From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:05:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: allocate the NPU TXD spaces only with an NPU

A driver built with NPU support allocates the TXD spaces for the NPU
on every board, also on a board without an NPU. The spaces take more
than 1 MiB of coherent memory, and only the NPU uses them.

Skip the allocation when no NPU is present. The NPU setup that reads
the spaces already stops without an NPU.

Fixes: e826923c533a ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: Store DMA mapped buffer addresses in mt7996_npu_hw_init()")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/npu.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/npu.c
+++ b/mt7996/npu.c
@@ -562,6 +562,9 @@ int mt7996_npu_hw_init(struct mt7996_dev
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr) % 3);
 
+	if (!mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76))
+		return 0;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dev->npu_txd_addr); i += 3) {
 		int band = i && is_mt7996(&dev->mt76) ? MT_BAND2 : MT_BAND0;
 		u32 size = is_mt7996(&dev->mt76) ? band == MT_BAND2
